preConditionHook:
// BULL LEDGE: at least `minMatches` of the last `lookback` bars have a low
// within toleranceTicks of THE CURRENT BAR'S low -- a small trading range with a
// flat floor. Short is the bear ledge, a flat ceiling of matching highs.
//
// ANCHORED AT THE CURRENT BAR, NOT PAIRWISE. Two of Brooks's four statements
// define the ledge pairwise (any two bars in the window matching each other),
// which is O(n^2) and can fire on a level price is nowhere near now; the third
// anchors the count at the current bar. The anchored reading wins on
// mechanizability and because it only fires while price is AT the ledge, which
// is what an entry needs.
//
// THE COUNT INCLUDES THE CURRENT BAR, which trivially matches itself, exactly as
// CountIF counts bars 0..N-1 inclusive. So minMatches = 2 means one OTHER bar
// shares the level, and minMatches = 1 is vacuously true.
//
// WRITTEN AS A LOOP, NOT CountIF, and this is a specification point rather than
// a style choice: CountIF's condition is a true SERIES whose offsets shift with
// the counted bar (measured), so both the price read and any variable holding the anchor
// would shift too and the test would degenerate to the distance from a bar to itself,
// which is 0 on every bar. An anchored count cannot be expressed with CountIF.
//
// Tolerance 0 is Brooks's literal 'identical lows' and is the default; one
// source says a tick. Tick division-first into a local. The entry offset of
// R28-23 (a limit a tick or two above the ledge bottom) is not representable
// under the signal-bar-close / next-open convention and is not carried.
//
// NOT MicroDoubleExtreme, which requires the match at exactly `gap`; this accepts
// it at any lag inside the window. At lookback 2 / minMatches 2 the two coincide.
//
// The count is compared through el_ge against the input, mirroring EL, where
// every numeric is a float and >= carries the relational tolerance. Every
// scratch value is a localVariables entry, never a hook-scope declaration, so
// the hooks survive a double placement.
//
// Deepest bar touched: lookback - 1.
tickSize = ctx.MinMove() / ctx.PriceScale();
nMatchLow = 0;
nMatchHigh = 0;
for (ii = 0; ii <= (int)lookback - 1; ++ii) {
    if (el_le(std::fabs(low[ii] - low[0]), toleranceTicks * tickSize)) nMatchLow = nMatchLow + 1;
    if (el_le(std::fabs(high[ii] - high[0]), toleranceTicks * tickSize)) nMatchHigh = nMatchHigh + 1;
}
